Z||000000||artherd||10-30-2001||04:02 AM||||... That is the Question!  Wether tis nobeler to go with the more widely available (and certinly very decent) lubericant, or suffer the sligs and arrows of mail-order, and then keep a few in the trunk, all just to have something that says "abuse your engine" on the bottle.  And is easier to pour.  And cool-looking.<P>For a 2.8?  For something a little bigger (4.6) and cammier (4 of them, in a DOHC Vee setup?)<P>Anyone?<BR>Beuler?<BR>Anyone?<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||RossT||10-30-2001||04:29 AM||||I used to use nothing but amsoil dating back to the late 70's.  But it became a big hassel trying to get it when you need it.  They also kept raising their prices, so I converted to mobil-1 about 2 years ago.  Twice a year Walmart runs a 5 quart jug for<BR>$17.88.  At that price I stock up with a years supply.  <P>I change the oil twice a year and the filter every 3 months.<P>I use hastings premium oil fiters.  They are the company that makes amsoil their filters, but at 1/3 the cost, it just says hastings not amsoil on it.  The insides are identical!<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 10-30-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-30-2001||09:02 AM||||YEAH!! another AmsOil buff!!  rock on!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i've beat the CRAP out of my GT and it's still ticking! not 100% sure it's the lubricant or what but i know  my SE didn't hold up as well with Royal Purple and Mobile one... ||||reg||1
