Z||000006||Master_Sushi||10-30-2001||03:34 PM||||I've allways used mobil one in cars I care about. I used it in my 88 coupe and changed it every 3k miles. That thing ran great. I even overheated into the red zone with it. If I had crude in it then, my engine would probably be toast.<BR>Heres a good article some guy wrote up on Redline Vs Mobil 1. He used both for a while and send the old oil away for testing. He seems to know what hes talking about. You have to read from the bottom of the page to the top. Oh, and keep an open mind because its not a fiero he drives  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<BR> <A HREF="http://cjsupra.kendra.com/Oil-Spec.html" TARGET=_blank>http://cjsupra.kendra.com/Oil-Spec.html</A> ||||reg||14
